index_concurrent.rs hardcodes the refresh-lock path (.wiki/wiki-refresh.lock) to hold it externally and prove a second process serves without blocking. This path must match the one lock.rs#try_acquire actually locks. If lock.rs changes the filename or directory, the test would create a stale file at the old path while the binary locks elsewhere — the non-blocking assertions still pass, so the drift is silent (false confidence), not caught.
